# PRs and git

- Branch per task. Small PRs, one intent, under ~400 changed lines when possible.
- Conventional titles: `feat|fix|test|docs|refactor|chore|perf(scope): summary`.
- PR body sections (required): What · Why · How verified (exact commands + trimmed output) · Numbers changed (before → after + command) · Risks · Not done / follow-ups.
- Attach artifacts for anything visual or behavioral (screenshot, short video, eval table).
- Never force-push shared branches, rewrite history, tag, or publish. A human merges.
- The shell guard's matcher includes `git pull`. It blocks `git pull --rebase` (any `rebase`) and allows a plain `git pull`. It blocks force-push and `reset --hard` even when the flag is not next to the subcommand.
- Address every Bugbot finding: fix it or reply with a reason. Don't silently resolve.
